      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "You can now read provision questions as stock-accounting problems.\n\nFirst remove what was consumed before the change. Then use consumers × ration × remaining days for the leftover stock.\n\nReinforcements shorten supply life; people leaving extend it; smaller rations extend it too.\n\nNext, we apply chain rule to machines, production and physical job dimensions.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
